    <statement><p>Calculate the length of the path over the given interval.
<me>(\sin 2 t, \cos 2 t), \, 0 \le t \le \pi</me></p>
<p><fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2\pi </m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>x = \sin 2 t, \, y = \cos 2 t</m>, hence <m>x' = 2 \cos 2 t</m> and <m>y' = - 2 \sin 2 t</m>.  By the formula for the arc length we obtain:
<me>S = \int ^\pi _0 \sqrt{x'(t)^2 + y'(t)^2} \, dt = \int ^\pi _0 \sqrt{4 \cos^2 2 t + 4 \sin^2 2 t} \, dt = \int ^\pi _0 \sqrt{4} \, dt = 2 \pi</me>


</solution>
